; Stage 14 LW-1/LW-2 negative fixture: ambiguity under argument widening.
;
; `f` is overloaded on two integer widths, neither of which is `i32` — so a
; plain literal argument (whose own type defaults to i32) does not exact-match
; either candidate. Both `x:i64` and `x:ui8` reach the call at the tier-2
; widen/untyped-int-literal adaptation pool (LW-1's shared
; generic-resolve-adapt-tier), and a literal adapts to any integer type it
; fits (arg-adapts, src/generics.nuc), so the call is genuinely ambiguous.
; This proves the tier-2 ambiguity accounting still dies rather than silently
; picking a candidate (design/stage14/int-widening.md §1.1/§3 LW-1).
;
; Compiling this must FAIL with:
;   "ambiguous overload for 'f' under argument widening"

(defn f (x:i64):i32 (return (unsafe/cast i32 x)))
(defn f (x:ui8):i32 (return (as i32 x)))

(defn main ():i32
  (return (f 5)))
